const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Why is my Scotsman ice machine not making ice?",
    a: "A Scotsman ice machine that stopped making ice usually comes down to one of three things: a water-side fault (closed inlet, scaled inlet valve, clogged supply filter, or a failing spray pump — Scotsman-specific service item on Prodigy ELITE horizontal evaporator architecture), a sensor or harvest-timing failure stopping the cycle, or a refrigerant-side problem (low charge, weak compressor, fouled condenser). Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair work the diagnostic cheapest-first because about 4 in 5 Scotsman no-production calls in LA, OC, Ventura, and the IE land on water-side or spray-pump issues before refrigerant work is needed. $120 commercial diagnostic, applied toward repair."
  },
  {
    q: "What does E01 mean on my Scotsman Prodigy ELITE?",
    a: "E01 on a Scotsman Prodigy ELITE alphanumeric display means long freeze cycle — the freeze cycle exceeded its design time. Three usual causes in order of frequency: condenser fouling restricting heat rejection (most common, $245 to $385 cleaning), refrigerant under-charge from a slow leak ($700 to $1,500 EPA 608 leak repair plus recharge), or spray pump weakness reducing water flow across the horizontal evaporator. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair check head pressure on manifold gauges and inspect the condenser first because that resolves the majority of E01 calls. The AutoAlert system stores the fault for review during the diagnostic visit."
  },
  {
    q: "What does E04 mean on my Scotsman Prodigy ELITE?",
    a: "E04 on the Prodigy ELITE means no water sensed at the freeze chamber. Three usual causes: water supply shut off or partially closed at the wall valve, water filter cartridge clogged (Pentair Everpure or 3M Cuno on most Scotsman installs, 6-month replacement cycle), or the water inlet valve has failed closed. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair check the supply valve and filter first because those resolve roughly 4 of every 10 E04 calls at no parts cost. Water inlet valve replacement runs $260 to $420 if the upstream supply side checks clean."
  },
  {
    q: "What does E08 mean on my Scotsman Prodigy ELITE?",
    a: "E08 means water pump short cycling — the spray pump is running but not completing its expected duty cycle. This is a Scotsman-specific code because horizontal evaporator architecture uses a spray pump (water held in a sump below the evaporator, sprayed UP onto the evaporator surface by an electric pump) that vertical-evap competitors like Manitowoc don't have. Usual causes: spray pump impeller wear (year 6 to 9 typical Scotsman service item), spray nozzle clogged with scale, or low water level in the sump triggering pump protection. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair inspect the spray pump first because that's the dominant E08 root cause — spray pump replacement runs $380 to $540."
  },
  {
    q: "How do I reset my Scotsman Prodigy ELITE?",
    a: "Prodigy ELITE reset is a power-cycle plus AutoAlert sequence: turn off at the main breaker, wait 60 seconds, restore power. The AutoAlert display clears the active E-code. If the underlying fault is still present, the code returns within minutes (faster on serious faults like E05 high refrigerant pressure, slower on intermittent E04 water issues). Resetting without diagnosing is fine as a temporary workaround while you wait for our visit; don't ignore a code that keeps returning. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair note whether the AutoAlert code was intermittent or steady because that distinction points to different parts."
  },
  {
    q: "What's the difference between Scotsman Prodigy ELITE and Brilliance?",
    a: "Different ice types and architectures. Prodigy ELITE is Scotsman's flagship cube ice line with horizontal evaporator and spray pump architecture: C0322 (300 lb/day modular), C0530 (500 lb/day), C0630 (600 lb/day), C0830 (800 lb/day), C1030 (1,000 lb/day), C1448 (1,400 lb/day large modular). Brilliance is Scotsman's nugget ice line that pioneered the commercial 'Sonic ice' category: N0422 (420 lb/day), N0622 (620 lb/day), N0922 (920 lb/day) — competitors Hoshizaki Sliver Nugget and Manitowoc R-Series came after. Different failure modes: Prodigy ELITE fails on spray pump and AutoAlert sensors; Brilliance fails on auger gear reducer and extrusion mechanism (the signature Brilliance technology). Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair service both lines."
  },
  {
    q: "How long does a Scotsman ice machine repair take?",
    a: "Time-to-restoration depends on the failure category. Cleaning service: 90 minutes to 2 hours, same-day production restored. Water inlet valve: 60 to 90 minutes on-site, same-day. Spray pump replacement (Scotsman-specific): 90 to 120 minutes, same-day. AutoAlert sensor: 60 to 90 minutes, same-day. Condenser fan motor: 60 to 90 minutes, same-day. Brilliance extrusion mechanism: 2 to 3 hours, same-day if on truck; otherwise 1 to 3 day Vernon Hills expedite. Refrigerant leak repair: 3 to 5 hours including leak detection, evacuation, and recharge. AutoAlert board: same-day if on the truck; otherwise 4 to 7 day standard Ali Group ship. Common Prodigy ELITE parts (spray pumps, water inlet valves, AutoAlert sensors, harvest cycle solenoids) are stocked on the van for first-visit completion."
  },
  {
    q: "How much does Scotsman ice machine repair cost?",
    a: "Diagnostic visit $120, waived with repair. Typical repair line items: cleaning service $200 to $340; water filter $80 to $180; water inlet valve $260 to $420; spray pump replacement (Scotsman-specific) $380 to $540; AutoAlert harvest sensor $200 to $340; condenser coil cleaning $245 to $385; condenser fan motor $300 to $520; AutoAlert control board $480 to $820; extrusion mechanism (Brilliance nugget) $480 to $780; auger gear reducer (Brilliance) $580 to $880; refrigerant leak repair plus recharge $700 to $1,500; compressor replacement (undercounter and mid-size) $1,400 to $2,200; compressor replacement (C1030 and larger modular) $1,800 to $2,800. Most no-production calls resolve in the $260 to $540 range when the diagnostic points to water inlet, spray pump, or harvest-side work."
  },
  {
    q: "How often should a Scotsman ice machine be cleaned?",
    a: "Scotsman and LA County DPH recommend 2 to 4 cleanings per year on Prodigy ELITE and Brilliance machines — closer to 4 (quarterly) in heavy-use restaurants and bars with hard water, closer to 2 (every 6 months) in lighter-use settings with quality filtration. The horizontal spray pump architecture is particularly scale-sensitive because mineral deposits in the spray nozzles disrupt the spray pattern, leading to uneven ice formation before total production failure. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair document each service for LA County DPH inspection records. Standard cleaning runs $200 to $340 per service; quarterly contracts reduce per-cleaning cost."
  },
  {
    q: "Why does my Scotsman ice machine keep stopping mid-cycle?",
    a: "Mid-cycle shutdowns on a Scotsman Prodigy ELITE usually trigger one of two AutoAlert codes: E05 (high refrigerant pressure — compressor overheating from fouled condenser or restricted airflow, common when kitchen ambient exceeds 90°F during LA summer service) or E01 (long freeze cycle, cycle timer exceeded design, often refrigerant under-charge). Less commonly, E08 (water pump short cycling) triggers protection mid-cycle when the spray pump is failing intermittently. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair check the condenser fin condition first because that's the most common root cause on chain restaurant installations — $245 to $385 cleaning, $300 to $520 if a fan motor replacement is also needed."
  },
  {
    q: "Where can I get Scotsman parts in LA?",
    a: "Scotsman parts route through the Ali Group / Vernon Hills, Illinois service network: standard 5 to 7 day ship to LA, expedited 1 to 3 day available for service-critical components. Common Prodigy ELITE parts (spray pumps, water inlet valves, AutoAlert harvest sensors, harvest cycle solenoids, condenser fan motors for -A air-cooled units) are stocked on our service trucks for first-visit completion on most LA County hospitality calls. Brilliance nugget-specific parts (extrusion mechanisms, auger gear reducers for N0422/N0622/N0922) require Vernon Hills order. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair pre-order based on phone-call symptom description to compress restoration time."
  }
